<article class="env-lemma" id="08W7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08W7">Lemma <span data-tag="08W7">99.5.8</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[d] \ar[r]_ i &  X' \ar[d] \\  T \ar[r] &  T' }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a cartesian square of algebraic spaces where $T \to T'$ is a first order thickening. Let $\mathcal{F}'$ be an $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-module flat over $T'$. Set $\mathcal{F} = i^*\mathcal{F}'$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}'$ is a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-module of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}'$ is an $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-module of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that a finitely presented module is quasi-coherent hence the equivalence of (1) and (2) and (3) and (4). The equivalence of (2) and (4) is a special case of Deformation Theory, Lemma <a href="/tag/08VU" data-tag="08VU">91.11.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>